KG42.register("rules-4b8f33ae6e8ef5cecbbfde36",{"id":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R002","paper":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R002","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The cooling-air clearing price supplies the signal converted into the cooling-temperature set point through the price-to-set-point mapping. Scope: Central-HVAC air markets; conversion of cooling-air clearing prices into cooling-temperature set points. In these reported cases, the market clearing price \\hat{\\lambda} produces the same cooling-temperature set points as baseline operation. Scope: Reported central-system operating example with baseline-equivalent cooling-temperature set points. Condition: The supply/demand intersection price is below \\hat{\\lambda}, or there is no intersection. TC sets the market clearing price to its lowest value to set all zones' cooling-temperature set points to their minima, with the stated objective of consuming as much power as possible. Scope: Reported central-HVAC load-following case with insufficient power flexibility. Condition: The studied building lacks sufficient power flexibility for demand following. TC limits shared information to preserve customer privacy while using electricity price as its coordination signal. Scope: Price-based transactive coordination for DR services. The default k is zero, meaning no DR service; a mechanism allowing occupants to update k can be integrated into thermostats. Scope: Central-HVAC price-to-set-point design and its optional thermostat interface. TC is active only during occupied periods. The market period is five minutes, and simulated set points are updated every five minutes. Scope: Reported central-HVAC building-energy simulation configuration. Use T_{set,base} as the default cooling-temperature set point. Scope: Reported central-HVAC real time price and load following service configurations. Condition: The supply and demand curves have no intersection.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["ev-v141-b-g03-013","v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g04-E01","v141-b-g04-E02"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Central-HVAC air markets; conversion of cooling-air clearing prices into cooling-temperature set points. | Central-HVAC price-to-set-point design and its optional thermostat interface. | Price-based transactive coordination for DR services. | Reported central-HVAC building-energy simulation configuration. | Reported central-HVAC load-following case with insufficient power flexibility. | Reported central-HVAC real time price and load following service configurations. | Reported central-system operating example with baseline-equivalent cooling-temperature set points.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["ev-v141-b-g03-013","v141-b-g01-e01","v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g02-E034","v141-b-g02-E037","v141-b-g04-E01","v141-b-g04-E02"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"x_T_set","symbol":"T^{i,j}_{set,t}","meaning":"Cooling-temperature set point of the i-th zone served by the j-th AHU at time t; the output of the price-to-set-point mapping.","kind":"operational","domain":"Source-defined cooling-temperature set point values; explicit numeric bounds are not stated in the source.","unit":"°C","indices":["i","j","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e09"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta_T_set_base","symbol":"T_{set,base}","meaning":"Cooling-temperature set point under normal condition; also used as the default set point when supply and demand curves have no intersection.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"°C","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g02-E037"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_Delta_T","symbol":"\\Delta T","meaning":"Relaxation bound for the cooling-temperature set point; set to 1.11 °C in the reported case-study configuration.","value":{"kind":"numeric","number_value":1.11,"text_value":null},"unit":"°C","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g02-E034"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_k","symbol":"k","meaning":"Dimensionless occupant preference for thermal comfort versus DR participation; default value 0. In the reported case study it is randomly selected in [0,1] for each zone and held constant over the control period.","value":{"kind":"numeric","number_value":0.0,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g02-E034"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_t","symbol":"\\lambda_t","meaning":"Electricity price at time t used as the price signal in Eq. (1).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"price unit (not explicitly stated)","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_hat_mean","symbol":"\\hat{\\lambda}","meaning":"Mean value of the electricity price during a previous period (e.g., the last 24 hours) as defined for Eq. (1); this is not the market-clearing-price symbol used in C002.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"price unit (not explicitly stated)","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_sigma","symbol":"\\sigma","meaning":"Standard deviation of the electricity price during a previous period as defined for Eq. (1).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"price unit (not explicitly stated)","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_market_period","symbol":"market period","meaning":"Interval for updating cooling-temperature set points; reported as 5 minutes for both HVAC systems.","value":{"kind":"numeric","number_value":5.0,"text_value":null},"unit":"min","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E034"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_update_interval","symbol":"set-point update interval","meaning":"Interval for updating simulated set points in the building-energy simulations; reported as 5 minutes.","value":{"kind":"numeric","number_value":5.0,"text_value":null},"unit":"min","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E034"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The cooling-air clearing price supplies the signal converted into the cooling-temperature set point through the price-to-set-point mapping. Scope: Central-HVAC air markets; conversion of cooling-air clearing prices into cooling-temperature set points.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"In these reported cases, the market clearing price \\hat{\\lambda} produces the same cooling-temperature set points as baseline operation. Scope: Reported central-system operating example with baseline-equivalent cooling-temperature set points. Condition: The supply/demand intersection price is below \\hat{\\lambda}, or there is no intersection.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["ev-v141-b-g03-013"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"TC sets the market clearing price to its lowest value to set all zones' cooling-temperature set points to their minima, with the stated objective of consuming as much power as possible. Scope: Reported central-HVAC load-following case with insufficient power flexibility. Condition: The studied building lacks sufficient power flexibility for demand following.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E01","v141-b-g04-E02"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"TC limits shared information to preserve customer privacy while using electricity price as its coordination signal. Scope: Price-based transactive coordination for DR services.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e01"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The default k is zero, meaning no DR service; a mechanism allowing occupants to update k can be integrated into thermostats. Scope: Central-HVAC price-to-set-point design and its optional thermostat interface.","expression":"k = 0 \\text{ (default)}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e14"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"TC is active only during occupied periods. The market period is five minutes, and simulated set points are updated every five minutes. Scope: Reported central-HVAC building-energy simulation configuration.","expression":"\\text{market period} = 5\\ \\mathrm{min};\\ \\text{set-point update interval} = 5\\ \\mathrm{min}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_market_period","theta_update_interval"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E034"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Use T_{set,base} as the default cooling-temperature set point. Scope: Reported central-HVAC real time price and load following service configurations. Condition: The supply and demand curves have no intersection.","expression":"T^{i,j}_{set,t} = T_{set,base} \\quad \\text{if no supply-demand intersection}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x_T_set"],"parameter_refs":["theta_T_set_base"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E037"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C008","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Equation (1) defines the price-to-set-point mapping used for the air market: the cooling-temperature set point of the i-th zone served by the j-th AHU at time t is set according to the electricity price relative to its previous-period mean and standard deviation, with occupant preference k and relaxation bound ΔT. Scope: Air-market price-to-set-point mapping in central-HVAC transactive control.","expression":"T^{i,j}_{set,t} = \\begin{cases} T_{set,base} - k\\Delta T, & \\text{if } \\lambda_t \u003c \\hat{\\lambda} - \\sigma, \\\\ T_{set,base} + k\\Delta T, & \\text{else if } \\lambda_t > \\hat{\\lambda} + \\sigma, \\\\ T_{set,base} - k\\Delta T + \\Delta T \\frac{k(\\lambda_t - \\hat{\\lambda} + \\sigma)}{\\sigma}, & \\text{otherwise}. \\end{cases}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x_T_set"],"parameter_refs":["theta_T_set_base","theta_Delta_T","theta_k","theta_lambda_t","theta_lambda_hat_mean","theta_sigma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g02-E010"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"ev-v141-b-g03-013","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p11-c2r2__v141-a-M01-activation","page":11,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"4.3.2. Demand limiting Fig. 16 illustrates performance of the TC approach when providing the demand ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 17","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-11.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In addition, for a significant period of time (e.g., from 6:00 to 10:00 a.m.), the power of the central system under the TC approach is the same as the baseline power. This is because either (1) the price of the intersection between the supply curve and the demand curve is less than \\hat{\\lambda} or (2) there is no intersection. In both cases, \\hat{\\lambda} is the market clearing price resulting in the same cooling temperature set points as those of the baseline operation, as illustrated in Fig. 17."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e01","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p01-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"the electricity price as the control signal to coordinate and achieve distinct objectives. It has tw","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In particular, TC uses the electricity price as the control signal to coordinate and achieve distinct objectives. It has two advantages: (1) it offers a scalable, distributed mechanism to address the conflicting operation objectives when providing DR services, and (2) it preserves customer privacy by limiting the information that can be shared."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-activation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"g y q y g m- of the price. • Step 3: Set Point Update This step converts the clearing price of the c","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Step 3: Set Point Update\nThis step converts the clearing price of the cooling air into the cooling temperature set point based on the price to set point mapping. With the updated cooling temperature set point, the local control loop for maintaining the zone temperature adjusts the supply of cooling air to realize the clearing quantity of each zone and consequently realize the total clearing quantity in each market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"he p p ; 𝑡 y p ; he are the mean value and the standard deviation, respectively, of the es electrici","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"• A larger k means the occupants are sensitive to the price and willing to participate in the DR services.\n• A small k means the occupants are more concerned about the thermal comfort.\n• The default value of k is 0, meaning no DR service.\n• A mechanism for occupants to update k can be integrated into the thermostats."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E034","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p09-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2.1. Market instantiation","anchor_text":"every 1 min. On the other hand, the NAE sends the set points to the A FCs which then actuate the set","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"For both HVAC systems, the market period is 5 minutes, and the set points in the building energy simulations are updated every 5 minutes. In addition, TC is active only during the occupied period. The value of k for each zone is randomly selected between the range from 0 to 1 and is assumed to be constant over the entire control period. In addition, the value of \\Delta T for each zone is set to be 1.11 °C."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E037","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M02-validation","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2.1. Market instantiation","anchor_text":"𝑘 is he imposed on the studied HVAC systems to fully ‘‘excite’’ the system. in Then, based on buildi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"In addition, for the real time price and the load following, there may not be an intersection between the supply and demand curves. In this case, T_{set,base} is used as the default value of the set point."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p12-c1r4__v141-a-M01-activation","page":12,"printed_page":"12","section":"4.3.3. Load following","anchor_text":"challenging without sub-meters. po po 4.3.3. Load following 5 Fig. 19 illustrates the performance of","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"This occurs when the studied building does not have sufficient power flexibility for demand following."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E02","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p12-c1r4__v141-a-M01-activation","page":12,"printed_page":"12","section":"4.3.3. Load following","anchor_text":"challenging without sub-meters. po po 4.3.3. Load following 5 Fig. 19 illustrates the performance of","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In such a case, the proposed TC approach sets the market clearing price to the lowest value so that the cooling temperature set points of all zones are set to be the minimum to consume as much power as possible."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"no conversion of demand curves is needed, as shown in Fig. 7. The supply curve of the electricity ma","equation_id":"Eq. (1)","figure_id":"Fig. 8","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"T^{i,j}_{set,t} = { T_{set,base} − kΔT, if λ_t \u003c λ̂ − σ; T_{set,base} + kΔT, else if λ_t > λ̂ + σ; T_{set,base} − kΔT + ΔT · [k(λ_t − λ̂ + σ)/σ], otherwise } (1). where T^{i,j}_{set,t} is the cooling temperature set point of the ith zone served by the jth AHU at time t; T_{set,base} is the cooling temperature set point under the normal condition; ΔT is the relaxation bound for the cooling temperature set point; λ_t is the electricity price at time t; λ̂ and σ are the mean value and the standard deviation, respectively, of the electricity price during a previous period (e.g., the last 24 hours); and k is dimensionless, representing the building occupants’ preference of thermal comfort, and is to engage the participation of occupants in the DR services, as shown in Fig. 8."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E010","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3.1. Air market","anchor_text":"no conversion of demand curves is needed, as shown in Fig. 7. The supply curve of the electricity ma","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":"Fig. 8","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"T^{i,j}_{set,t} = \\begin{cases} T_{set,base} - k\\Delta T, & \\text{if } \\lambda_t \u003c \\hat{\\lambda} - \\sigma. \\\\ T_{set,base} + k\\Delta T, & \\text{else if } \\lambda_t > \\hat{\\lambda} + \\sigma. \\\\ T_{set,base} - k\\Delta T + \\Delta T \\frac{k(\\lambda_t - \\hat{\\lambda} + \\sigma)}{\\sigma}, & \\text{otherwise.} \\end{cases} \\quad (1)\nwhere T^{i,j}_{set,t} is the cooling temperature set point of the i-th zone served by the j-th AHU at time t; T_{set,base} is the cooling temperature set point under the normal condition; \\Delta T is the relaxation bound for the cooling temperature set point; \\lambda_t is the electricity price at time t; \\hat{\\lambda} and \\sigma are the mean value and the standard deviation, respectively, of the electricity price during a previous period (e.g., the last 24 hours); and k is dimensionless, representing the building occupants' preference of thermal comfort, and is to engage the participation of occupants in the DR services, as shown in Fig. 8."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-activation","v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-validation","v141-a-M02-activation","v141-a-M02-participation","v141-a-M02-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e09","quote":"This step converts the clearing price of the cooling air into the cooling temperature set point based on the price to set point mapping."}],[{"evidence_id":"ev-v141-b-g03-013","quote":"This is because either (1) the price of the intersection between the supply curve and the demand curve is less than \\hat{\\lambda} or (2) there is no intersection. In both cases, \\hat{\\lambda} is the market clearing price resulting in the same cooling temperature set points as those of the baseline operation"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E02","quote":"In such a case, the proposed TC approach sets the market clearing price to the lowest value so that the cooling temperature set points of all zones are set to be the minimum to consume as much power as possible."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E01","quote":"This occurs when the studied building does not have sufficient power flexibility for demand following."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e01","quote":"TC uses the electricity price as the control signal to coordinate and achieve distinct objectives."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e01","quote":"it preserves customer privacy by limiting the information that can be shared."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e14","quote":"The default value of k is 0, meaning no DR service."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e14","quote":"A mechanism for occupants to update k can be integrated into the thermostats."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E034","quote":"For both HVAC systems, the market period is 5 minutes, and the set points in the building energy simulations are updated every 5 minutes. In addition, TC is active only during the occupied period."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E037","quote":"In addition, for the real time price and the load following, there may not be an intersection between the supply and demand curves. In this case, T_{set,base} is used as the default value of the set point."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"f5eb519a2f4e33a60510ff49887bea5f3fb18af4cd374602e75456af164ef89f","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The core price-to-set-point mapping is transcribed from Eq. (1), and explicit default/timing constants are formalized from the supplied source evidence. Several procedural branches (C001-C004) remain qualitative, and source notation conflicts and missing bounds are flagged in revision_requests.","bindings":[{"object_id":"x_T_set","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The cooling-temperature set point is the output of the price-to-set-point conversion at coordination.price_signal, fed by pricing.local through edge E001."},{"object_id":"theta_T_set_base","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Baseline set point parameter used in the price-to-set-point mapping and the no-intersection fallback at coordination.price_signal."},{"object_id":"theta_Delta_T","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Relaxation-bound parameter in the price-to-set-point mapping at coordination.price_signal."},{"object_id":"theta_k","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Occupant-preference parameter in the price-to-set-point mapping; the edge carries the price signal into that mapping."},{"object_id":"theta_lambda_t","node_ids":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Electricity price input in Eq. (1) is the price signal supplied by pricing.local to coordination.price_signal."},{"object_id":"theta_lambda_hat_mean","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Previous-period mean price parameter in Eq. (1); its scope is the mapping's price history at coordination.price_signal, not the clearing-price symbol in C002."},{"object_id":"theta_sigma","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Previous-period price-standard-deviation parameter in Eq. (1) at coordination.price_signal."},{"object_id":"theta_market_period","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Timing parameter for the coordination stage; the frozen graph has no timing edge representing the five-minute market period."},{"object_id":"theta_update_interval","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Timing parameter for simulated set-point updates; the frozen graph has no timing edge representing the five-minute update interval."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C005","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Default k=0 parameterizes the price-to-set-point mapping; edge E001 carries the price signal into that mapping."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C006","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The five-minute market period and update interval are timing conditions on coordination.price_signal; the frozen graph has no timing edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C007","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"The no-intersection fallback sets the output set point at coordination.price_signal to T_set,base; edge E001 carries the price signal into this stage."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R002-C008","node_ids":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R002-E001"],"rationale":"Eq. (1) is the price-to-set-point mapping at coordination.price_signal using the price signal from pricing.local; edge E001 links these nodes."}],"revision_requests":["C.1: clarify whether the price-to-set-point mapping in Eq. (1) uses the electricity price \\lambda_t or the cooling-air clearing price referenced in C001; the source text uses both phrasings and the frozen rule statement uses the latter.","C.1: disambiguate the symbol \\hat{\\lambda}: Eq. (1) defines it as the previous-period mean electricity price, while C002 and ev-v141-b-g03-013 use it as the market clearing price. Provide scoped symbols or confirm separate variables.","C.1: provide explicit lower bounds or domains for the 'lowest value' market clearing price and the 'minimum' cooling-temperature set points in C003; the source does not state numeric bounds or an optimization expression.","C.1: provide an explicit symbol or predicate for the no-intersection condition and, if C002 is to be formalized, the supply-demand intersection price p_int; the frozen graph has no node or edge representing the intersection price.","C.1: confirm whether the five-minute market period and five-minute set-point update interval in C006 are general rule parameters or case-study configuration values; currently they are treated as reported configuration parameters."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
